# How many Dux workers may run at once, across every registered repository.
# dux-spawn counts the tasks the ledger holds as running or stale and refuses
# a start at this number; the task stays queued until a worker finishes.
#
# Rounds (feedback, answers, approval) continue a session that was already
# admitted and are never refused for this, so the count can pass it while
# they run.
#
# 1 gives back one worker at a time.
#
# Copy this file to config/max-workers to change it: a whole number from 1 to
# 99. The installer seeds the value once and never edits one you wrote.
3
